~ start
Lunaris: So... the moon sends you? I am Lunaris, Warden of Reflection.  
Lunaris: Let us see if your reason shines even when the light fades.  
[do! get_tree().get_first_node_in_group("player").lock_player()]
[do! DialogueManager.lunaris.face_player()]
=> Q1

~ Q1
Lunaris: Solve the equation: 2cos(x) - 3 = 0  
- A. x = π/6 and x = 11π/6 => Q1_WRONG
- B. x = π/3 and x = 5π/3 => Q1_CORRECT
- C. x = 5π/6 and x = 7π/6 => Q1_WRONG
- D. x = π/4 and x = 7π/4 => Q1_WRONG

~ Q1_CORRECT
Lunaris: You see through the dark — correct. [do! DialogueManager.lunaris.trigger_correct_answer()]
=> Q2

~ Q1_WRONG
Lunaris: The numbers mock your uncertainty. [do! DialogueManager.lunaris.trigger_wrong_answer()]
=> END

~ Q2
Lunaris: For 2sin(x) + 1 = 0, find all possible x.  
- A. x = 3π/4 and x = 5π/4 => Q2_WRONG
- B. x = 5π/4 and x = 7π/4 => Q2_CORRECT
- C. x = π/4 and x = 7π/4 => Q2_WRONG
- D. x = 7π/6 and x = 11π/6 => Q2_WRONG

~ Q2_CORRECT
Lunaris: As gentle as moonlight, yet exact. [do! DialogueManager.lunaris.trigger_correct_answer()]
=> Q3

~ Q2_WRONG
Lunaris: Even shadows can mislead. [do! DialogueManager.lunaris.trigger_wrong_answer()]
=> END

~ Q3
Lunaris: Simplify: 5tan(x) + 5 = 0  
- A. x = 3π/4 + 2kπ => Q3_WRONG
- B. x = 3π/4 + kπ => Q3_CORRECT
- C. x = π/4 + kπ => Q3_WRONG
- D. x = 5π/4 + 2kπ => Q3_WRONG

~ Q3_CORRECT
Lunaris: Good. The tangent bows to your will. [do! DialogueManager.lunaris.trigger_correct_answer()]
=> Q4

~ Q3_WRONG
Lunaris: The reflection bends wrongly. [do! DialogueManager.lunaris.trigger_wrong_answer()]
=> END

~ Q4
Lunaris: Which trigonometric function reveals the horizontal distance of a light beam when its total length and angle are known?  
- A. Cosecant => Q4_WRONG
- B. Cosine => Q4_CORRECT
- C. Sine => Q4_WRONG
- D. Tangent => Q4_WRONG

~ Q4_CORRECT
Lunaris: The mind mirrors the truth — correct. [do! DialogueManager.lunaris.trigger_correct_answer()]
=> Q5

~ Q4_WRONG
Lunaris: You chose the wrong reflection. [do! DialogueManager.lunaris.trigger_wrong_answer()]
=> END

~ Q5
Lunaris: If a path extends east and north forming a right triangle, and its eastward component measures roughly 9.59° N of E, what is its bearing?  
- A. 9.46° N of E => Q5_WRONG
- B. 9.59° N of E => Q5_CORRECT
- C. 80.4° N of E => Q5_WRONG
- D. 80.54° N of E => Q5_WRONG

~ Q5_CORRECT
Lunaris: The stars align. You have passed the lunar trial. [do! DialogueManager.lunaris.trigger_death()]
[do! get_tree().get_first_node_in_group("player").unlock_player()]
[do! DialogueManager.lunaris.queue_free()]
=> END!

~ Q5_WRONG
Lunaris: The horizon escapes your sight. [do! DialogueManager.lunaris.trigger_wrong_answer()]
=> END
